    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9f23b477-350c-5f7e-ae9b-27a0a8d4e30b",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(A)=0$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is not invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=6 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=0$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<6$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{6}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $A\\text{ is not invertible}$. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false: $\\text{rank}(A)=6$. $\\text{rank}(A)<6$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\n- Statement III is true: $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and III only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
